{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a photoactive electron donor-acceptor (EDA) complex-induced chromium-catalyzed Nozaki-Hiyama-Kishi (NHK) reaction. By utilizing Hantzsch ester (HE) as both an electron donor for EDA complex formation with alkyl thianthrenium salts and a terminal reductant for chromium turnover, the method achieves alkyl addition to aldehydes without external metal reductants or expensive photocatalysts. A key feature is the synthesis of \u03b2-deuterated secondary alcohols using easily prepared \u03b1-deuterated alkyl thianthrenium salts.",
